<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Albret</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Albret was a noble family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>, named after the lordship of Albret in the Landes, which rose through marriage and royal service to become kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>. Jean d'Albret married Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-of-navarre">Catherine of Navarre</a> in 1484, and the family kept Lower Navarre and Béarn after Ferdinand of Aragon conquered the rest of the kingdom in 1512. Through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeanne-dalbret">Jeanne d'Albret</a> their lands passed to her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-albret.jpg" alt="House of Albret" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armoiries_Albret.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
